    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0145" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6211/280½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 26, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: I return the enclosed
                    reports of the alleged interview with Baron von Schoen.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d62-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I hope that if there is any proper way of opening the matter with the German
                    Ambassador, it may be opened. I feel with you that there can be no real doubt
                    about the substantial authenticity of the interview and I think it not only
                    desirable, but imperative, that this gentleman should not remain here.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d62-f1" n="4" xml:id="d62-f1-content">
